## Steps

### Step 1: Preserve identifier text for FieldAccess refs in resolver

Change the FieldAccess early return to populate `unresolved_name` instead of discarding it. No schema migration — the `unresolved_name` column already exists and accepts any TEXT.

```rust
// src/resolver.rs, line 51-56: change unresolved_name from None to Some
if matches!(r.context_kind, RefContextKind::Import | RefContextKind::FieldAccess) {
    return ResolvedRef {
        original: r.clone(),
        target_symbol_id: None,
        unresolved_name: Some(r.name.clone()),  // was: None
        skipped: true,
    };
}
```

**Contract check**: `unresolved_name IS NOT NULL` now includes FieldAccess/Import refs. Callers to audit:
- `conventions/pipeline.rs` callee_cache: filters `context_kind == \"call\"` first → safe
- `sutra_refs` display: shows ref names → improvement (previously these showed as nameless)
- Any `WHERE unresolved_name IS NOT NULL` queries → check they also filter context_kind

### Step 2: Add callee prefix parser

A helper that splits DART_EFFECT_PATTERNS prefixes into (package_root, optional_class_name):

```rust
// src/conventions/attributes.rs

/// Parse a Dart callee prefix into (package_root, optional_member_name).
/// "http::" → ("http", None) — any member access on this alias
/// "dart:io::File" → ("dart:io", Some("File")) — specific class from package
fn parse_dart_callee_prefix(prefix: &str) -> Option<(&str, Option<&str>)> {
    let mut parts = prefix.splitn(2, "::");
    let package = parts.next().filter(|s| !s.is_empty())?;
    let member = parts.next().filter(|s| !s.is_empty());
    Some((package, member))
}
```

### Step 3: Add Dart-specific effect enrichment function

```rust
// src/conventions/attributes.rs

use std::collections::HashSet;

/// Dart-specific: detect effects from import-derived package refs.
/// Handles two patterns:
/// A) Aliased calls (http.get) → FieldAccess ref name matches package name
/// B) Direct class use (File.open) → unresolved ref name matches class from package
pub fn enrich_with_dart_import_effects(
    sym_attrs: &mut SymbolAttrs,
    sym: &SymbolRow,
    file_refs: &[RefRow],
    import_packages: &HashSet<&str>,
    patterns: &[EffectPattern],
) {
    for pattern in patterns {
        if sym_attrs.attributes.contains(&pattern.attr_name.to_string()) {
            continue;
        }

        let matched = pattern.callee_prefixes.iter().any(|prefix| {
            let Some((package, member)) = parse_dart_callee_prefix(prefix) else {
                return false;
            };
            if !import_packages.contains(package) {
                return false;
            }
            file_refs.iter().any(|r| {
                if r.line < sym.start_line || r.line > sym.end_line {
                    return false;
                }
                let Some(ref name) = r.unresolved_name else {
                    return false;
                };
                match member {
                    None => r.context_kind == \"field_access\" && name == package,
                    Some(class) => name == class,
                }
            })
        });

        if matched {
            sym_attrs.attributes.push(pattern.attr_name.to_string());
        }
    }
}
```

